Task Tracker build scripts

This directory intentionally contains separate build scripts for different environments.

1. Common release build

File:
- scripts/build.mjs

Purpose:
- Build the plugin into dist/
- Include plugin.json, README.md, README_zh_CN.md, docs/, and i18n/
- Do not sync to any local SiYuan plugin directory

Use when:
- preparing GitHub release artifacts
- building on another computer
- you only want dist/ output

Command:
- npm run build


2. Local machine build

File:
- scripts/build.local.mjs

Purpose:
- Build the plugin into dist/
- Sync the built plugin to the local SiYuan plugin directory on this machine
- Keep README and i18n in the local plugin directory so the plugin remains fully usable locally

Local target priority:
- SIYUAN_PLUGIN_DIR environment variable, if set
- /Users/risoyo/LocalHDD/SiYuan/data/plugins/siyuan-plugin-task-tracker
- /Users/risoyo/SiYuan/data/plugins/siyuan-plugin-task-tracker

Command:
- SIYUAN_PLUGIN_DIR=/path/to/data/plugins/siyuan-plugin-task-tracker npm run build:local
- or just npm run build:local if one of the known local paths exists


3. Release packaging

File:
- scripts/release.mjs

Purpose:
- Run the common release build
- Create release/siyuan-plugin-task-tracker-v<version>.zip from dist/

Command:
- npm run release


4. When another machine has packaging or local sync issues

Suggested troubleshooting order:
- first read this file
- run npm run typecheck
- run npm run build
- confirm dist/ contains:
  - index.js
  - index.css
  - plugin.json
  - README.md
  - README_zh_CN.md
  - docs/
  - i18n/
- for local sync issues, set SIYUAN_PLUGIN_DIR to that machine's plugin directory and run npm run build:local

Important rule:
- do not force the release build script to support every machine
- keep scripts/build.mjs machine-independent for release packaging
- put machine-specific local sync configuration in SIYUAN_PLUGIN_DIR instead of polluting scripts/build.mjs
